    "note": "The Barlow train shed has one broad glazed vault above raised platforms, set against a low modern northern extension. The red-brick Midland Grand frontage adds a recessed entrance, stepped Gothic roofs and the Euston Road clock tower. The 17 m sea-level datum follows standard viewer terrain at the streets. The raised station deck has a stepped apron and open north underpass. The two named building outlines replace the station and adjoining hotel, along with three contained elevator parts. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
